Falsifies `xtask::swish_check::boot::swish_check_leg`, at the `caps` census line of its second boot
(`SWISH_CHECK_AFTER_REBOOT`) and its keyboard boot (`SWISH_CHECK_KEYBOARD_BOOT`, which the run does
not reach). Named for the leg rather than for `swish_check_boot`, whose one record name milestone
673's patch already holds, because the census lines run only on the leg's second and third boots.

Architecture: aarch64
Line: caps

Milestone 715 (the spawn service holds the display grants, and the shell holds none), row 32 of
notes/confinement-claims.md. `script/falsifications --sweep xtask` replays it (milestone 742 (every
test is falsified as routine), provisional): it boots `script/swish-check --arch aarch64` with this
patch applied and calls it red only when swish-check's FAILED report names the `Line:` above. By
hand, the same thing is:

    git apply xtask/falsifications/swish_check.boot.swish_check_leg.patch
    script/swish-check --arch aarch64        # must exit non-zero, failing `caps`
    git apply -R xtask/falsifications/swish_check.boot.swish_check_leg.patch

The defect is the progenitor placing copies of the gpu's four and the keyboard's three in the shell
at `spawnproto::SHELL_GPU_SLOT` onward, with `GRANT`, which is what it did from milestone 632
(graphics on demand) to milestone 715. The spawn service still holds its own, so launches keep
working; only the shell's table is wider.

Expected to fail: the second boot (a gpu, no keyboard) wants the census to end ` 21 62`, and the
shell reports `slots held: 0 1 2 3 4 5 20 21 22 23 24 25 62`. Replayed 2026-10-03 (UTC): exit 1
at that line; the fixed tree reads `slots held: 0 1 2 3 4 5 20 21 62` and exits 0 past it. (The
run-unvouched slot was 30 on that date and is 62 since milestone 754 (the capability table grows to 64 slots); the replay was not repeated.)
Re-cut 2026-10-12 (UTC) by the long-function paydown lane, when `boot` was split along its steps:
the same insertion, now in `boot` right after `finish_shell_endowment` places the machine page.
Re-cut 2026-10-18 (UTC) by lane/ioping-direct-io, when the second mounted tree became the disk
tree: the same insertion, against the new lines above it.

